{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342204,"nonce":"1fUIGuTZJM9tdxhQB0jJiSoLGqI=","title":"HIR value tables keep the capacity of the SSA phi transient, and every clone of a function copies it","message":"HirFunction::sweep_unreferenced_values retains the live values but never shrinks the IndexMap, and indexmap's Clone reserves entries up to the source's capacity. After SsaBuilder::build_from_typed_cfg fills incomplete phis and collapses them, a function keeps a value table sized for the transient: files.lua's main chunk holds 63,199 values with capacity 1,835,008 (about 470 MB at 256 B per bucket); nextvar's chunk$0 and chunk$3 hold about 11k values at capacity 114,688 (32 MB each); api's run at 1.5 to 3x. Every copy made afterwards (the scratch module, make_interp_body, optimize_body, recursive_inline, the LLVM input) allocates the inflated table again.\n\nEvidence (NUC, instrumented release zylua, counting allocator plus capacity census): files lowered module clone 505 MB of which values 483 MB; main-chunk SSA retains +523 MB. Experiment ZYNTAX_MEMX_SHRINK=1 (values.shrink_to_fit after the sweep), VmHWM over 2 rounds: files 996/1014 -\u003e 796/798 MB (LLVM 1073/1126 -\u003e 797/799), nextvar 349/355 -\u003e 279/286 (LLVM 416/413 -\u003e 329/335), api 269/265 -\u003e 256/255, bitwise and tokenize unchanged; wall unchanged. Module clone: files 505 -\u003e 68 MB, nextvar 110 -\u003e 52.5, api 146 -\u003e 130, bitwise 34 -\u003e 30. nextvar heap at exit 423 -\u003e 180 MB (interp_bodies 78 -\u003e 23, optimized_bodies 56 -\u003e 20).\n\nSavings: files about 200 MB peak RSS and 450 MB retained heap; nextvar 70 to 85 MB RSS; api about 12 MB.\n\nFix: shrink values (and blocks) at the end of sweep_unreferenced_values when len is under half the capacity, and give HirFunction a Clone that builds exact-size tables, so no copy inherits slack. Package MEM-hir-capacity.","files":null}]}